(a) In accordance with O.C.G.A. § 38-3-56, before building, constructing, repairing, renovating or making improvements to any real property, including dwellings, homes, buildings, structures or fixtures within an area in the unincorporated area of the county designated in a declared emergency or disaster, any person, firm, partnership, corporation or other entity must register with the McIntosh County Development Board and secure a building permit that is posted at the work site. Each day any such entity does business in the county without complying with this ordinance constitutes a separate offense.
